WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.900
In this walkthrough we'll find a deal
in the blotter, and open it for a
closer look, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:15.267
The Deal List is the blotter — every
trade the system holds, whatever the
product. It opens showing all of them.

3
00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:24.100
The filters across the top narrow the list
down. They combine, so you can work from a
broad view to a precise one without losing your place.

4
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:33.867
Filter by asset class to see only the fixed income
trades. The list updates in place, and the filter
stays visible so you always know what you are looking at.

5
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:42.833
Any column can also group the rows.
Grouping by status collects the deals
into buckets, each showing how many it holds.

6
00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:51.833
Groups open expanded. Collapse one to see
just the summary line, which is the
quickest way to read totals across a large blotter.

7
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:58.300
The same control opens it again, and the
grouping can be changed or cleared whenever you like.

8
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:06.533
Opening a deal brings up its own panel
beside the list, so you keep the
blotter and the detail on screen together.

9
00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:14.600
And when you already know what you are
after, universal search reaches the same
deal directly. A counterparty name is usually enough.

10
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:21.233
Picking a result opens that deal straight
away, without going through the blotter at all.

11
00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:28.933
That completes Finding Deals. Every surface
shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
